---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base wide pageClass="quiet-index-page" title="Spatial and GIS record" description="Selected spatial measurement, remote-sensing, and academic GIS work by Ian Helfrich.">
  <div class="quiet-shell">
    <header class="quiet-header">
      <div>
        <p class="quiet-label">Supporting record · geographic information science</p>
        <h1>Spatial and GIS work</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="quiet-lead">Spatial measurement enters my research when geography is part of the economic question. This page keeps current research separate from earlier academic portfolio work.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="record-section" aria-labelledby="research-linked">
      <p class="section-label">Current public research</p>
      <h2 id="research-linked">Spatial measures inside economic models</h2>
      <div class="record-pair">
        <article>
          <p class="record-meta">Preprint · 2025 · with Elizaveta Gonchar</p>
          <h3><a href="/research/gonchar-helfrich-2025-spotlight">Trade in the Spotlight</a></h3>
          <p>Annual population and night-light information are used to construct economically weighted distance for gravity models of trade.</p>
          <p class="limit">Limit: the preprint does not establish the planned transport-network extension or a completed global panel.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="record-meta">Published dissertation · Georgia Tech · 2024</p>
          <h3><a href="/research/helfrich-2024-dissertation">Redefining Trade Dynamics</a></h3>
          <p>The dissertation connects network position, within-country spatial heterogeneity, gravity econometrics, and optimal-transport theory.</p>
          <p class="limit">Limit: later papers and datasets retain their own public status and should be read separately.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section" aria-labelledby="academic-records">
      <p class="section-label">Earlier academic portfolio</p>
      <h2 id="academic-records">Course and group submissions</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">These artifacts document training and execution. They are presented as academic work, with no claim that they are peer-reviewed research or client engagements.</p>
      <ol class="artifact-list">
        <li>
          <div><span>Individual academic submission</span><strong>Texas snowstorm spatial analysis</strong><p>Geocoded utility-territory, outage, weather, and tract-level information assembled for a planning course project.</p></div>
          <a href="/portfolio/Helfrich_CP6521_FinalProject_Texas.pdf">Open PDF</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div><span>Group academic submission</span><strong>Visualization for planning</strong><p>A municipal planning dossier combining spatial analysis, design concepts, figures, and narrative. Collaborators are credited in the report.</p></div>
          <a href="/portfolio/CP6006_FinalSubmission_Report.pdf">Open PDF</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <figure>
            <img src="/portfolio/Helfrich_EnglishAveLiDAR2.jpg" alt="LiDAR-derived building identification map from an academic GIS exercise" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><span>Academic exercise</span><strong>LiDAR building identification</strong><p>A small pipeline exercise using elevation data to identify building footprints.</p></figcaption>
          </figure>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <aside class="closing-note">The <a href="/datasets/effdist-v2026">EffDist V2026 record</a> documents planned data work. It does not claim a completed release.</aside>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .quiet-shell { width: min(100%, 72rem); margin-inline: auto; }
  .quiet-header { display: grid; padding-block: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(18rem, .7fr); gap: 2rem 5rem; align-items: end; border-block: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .quiet-label, .section-label, .record-meta, .artifact-list span { color: var(--muted); font: 620 .68rem/1.5 var(--font-data); letter-spacing: .07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { max-width: 10ch; margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
  .quiet-lead { margin: 0; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .record-section { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .record-section h2 { max-width: 17ch; margin: .5rem 0 2rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .section-intro { max-width: 64ch; }
  .record-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--ef-ink); border: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .record-pair article { padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--ef-paper); }
  .record-pair h3 { margin: .5rem 0 1rem; font-size: 1.65rem; }
  .record-pair h3 a { color: var(--ef-ink); }
  .limit { margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--ef-oxide); }
  .artifact-list { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); list-style: none; }
  .artifact-list > li { margin: 0; padding-block: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .artifact-list > li:not(:last-child) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 1rem 3rem; }
  .artifact-list strong { display: block; margin-top: .3rem; font: 600 1.35rem/1.3 var(--font-display); }
  .artifact-list p { max-width: 65ch; margin: .4rem 0 0; }
  .artifact-list a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 44px; align-items: center; font: 650 .7rem/1.4 var(--font-data); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .artifact-list figure { display: grid; margin: 0; grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, .55fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem 3rem; align-items: center; }
  .artifact-list img { display: block; width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .closing-note { margin-block: 2rem; padding: 1.25rem 0 1.25rem 1.25rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--ef-oxide); }
  @media (max-width: 45rem) { .quiet-header, .record-pair, .artifact-list figure, .artifact-list > li:not(:last-child) { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
